/-!
# The extra full-Ree Weyl identity in binary matrices

The linear reflection interchanges source root 1 and source root 4. The
first relative-root matrix is computed from its three root factors; eleven
packed products then certify the literal conjugation equation. Each product
is checked in the kernel by `Thompson.BinaryMatrix.decode_mul`.

The local root-word calculation follows `ParabolicMarkedComparison.BinaryRelations`;
its private helpers are reproduced here to preserve that module's boundary.
Source: Shinoda (1975), pp.81–83; Parrott (1972), p.683.
-/

public section
namespace Tits.AmalgamRigidity.FullRee.SecondExtension.WeylVerification.BinaryCheck
open ReeF4.DerivedTits.Realization
open ReeF4.DerivedTits.Realization.TransportComparison
open ReeTwo.ParabolicMarkedComparison.Binary
open Thompson.BinaryMatrix

set_option maxRecDepth 10000
set_option Elab.async false

